  "scope_summary": "The user explicitly promoted the reviewed SX-VIS-063 terrain candidate; required official research, feasibility and adversarial review; approved the SX-VIS-061 board, SX-DEC-064 active-route lighting, Candidate 004 package validation, and on 2026-08-30 the Core Board v02 pixels, Godot implementation, translucent Build preview, smaller cargo marker, the final connected rail-network master v03, SX-DEC-065, Candidate 005 machine validation, then the six fixed SX-DEC-066 Route Book 01 stages and Candidate 006 machine validation. On 2026-08-31 the user also approved SX-DEC-067: six optional Route Book 02 maps with authored caution-track segments, waste cargo, cardinal-adjacent disposal-yard delivery, and blocked-cell wayside decorations, then the exact-machine Candidate 007 evidence continuation. The user then clarified the main title must be a world-fitting title treatment and authorized SX-DEC-068: one transparent rail/cargo wordmark candidate in the existing title consumer plus exact-machine Candidate 008 package evidence. The user then explicitly approved the wordmark pixels, its canonical promotion, and the replacement exact-machine Candidate 009 package evidence. On 2026-09-01 the user approved SX-DEC-069: transparent object-only replacements for the eight wayside/cargo/disposal candidates and distinct renderer-local caution-entry versus normal-speed-recovery feedback. SX-DEC-065 makes deterministic machine verification the primary validation route; five-person comprehension and player-experience studies are not required, while final user review remains separately recorded. This approval permits the exact protected current-canon/evidence owners listed above. It does not authorize new gameplay beyond SX-DEC-069, audio, locale beyond its four approved locales, progression, Base changes, T2/Issue #227 work, PR #174 mutation, a solver, or human/player/release evidence promotion."
